message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on the Nuwa Pen. I recall it was classified in heading 8543 as an electrical machine with individual functions, not in 9608 as a pen. The alternatives were 8471.60 (input units) and 8543.70. Because the pen writes on any surface and captures the strokes with an image sensor, then transmits them by Bluetooth, it works as a digitizer-style input device. I think the ruling went to 8543.70.9960, "Other: Other: Other", but I'm not certain.

The pen has a traditional ink writing function, which might point to 9608.10, but the electronic functions are the essential character. As an input unit for an ADP machine, it could fall under 8471.60.xx. However, the pen's own memory and its separate storing and transcribing functions argue against that, and Bluetooth transmission to a phone points to 8543.70. I'll go with 8543.70.9960.

{"hts_code": "8543.70.9960", "reason": "The rechargeable Bluetooth smart pen with image capture and internal memory is an electrical apparatus with individual functions not specified elsewhere, so it falls in heading 8543 rather than in the writing instruments of heading 9608."}
